<article class="env-lemma" id="0BB0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BB0">Lemma <span data-tag="0BB0">67.48.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$Y$ is Nagata, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is quasi-separated of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$ is reduced. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the normalization $\nu : Y' \to Y$ of $Y$ in $X$ is finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is étale local on $Y$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABP" data-tag="0ABP">67.48.4</a>. Thus we may assume $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is affine. Then $R$ is a Noetherian Nagata ring and we have to show that the integral closure of $R$ in $\Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ is finite over $R$. Since $f$ is quasi-compact we see that $X$ is quasi-compact. Choose an affine scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X$ (Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03H6" data-tag="03H6">66.6.3</a>). Then $\Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \subset \Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ X)$. Since $R$ is Noetherian it suffices to show that the integral closure of $R$ in $\Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)$ is finite over $R$. As $U \to Y$ is of finite type this follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/03GR" data-tag="03GR">29.54.15</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>